Subject: [PATCH] commander_core: retry the command on a transport timeout

The Commander family intermittently fails to answer within liquidctl's read
timeout, which surfaced as 'Error on CommanderCore:<channel>' plus a 500 from
coolercontrol-liqctld and left that channel on its previous duty for a poll
cycle. The existing retry loop only covers stray/incorrect reports; a Timeout
exception escaped it entirely.

Re-send the command up to three times with a 100ms backoff.  Re-writing is
required: once the device has dropped a response window, re-issuing the command is
the only thing that brings a reply back.  The invalid-report counter is
deliberately left alone here, so a transport retry never eats the 50-attempt
budget.

Each attempt costs the driver's 5000ms read timeout, so the worst case moves from
~5s (one timeout, fail fast) to ~20s (four reads plus the backoffs).  That is the
price of recovering a dropped window instead of losing the whole poll cycle.
---
--- a/commander_core.py
+++ b/commander_core.py
@@ -9,10 +9,16 @@
 """
 
 import logging
+import time
 from contextlib import contextmanager
 
 from liquidctl.driver.usb import UsbHidDriver
-from liquidctl.error import ExpectationNotMet, NotSupportedByDevice, NotSupportedByDriver
+from liquidctl.error import (
+    ExpectationNotMet,
+    NotSupportedByDevice,
+    NotSupportedByDriver,
+    Timeout,
+)
 from liquidctl.util import clamp, u16le_from
 
 _LOGGER = logging.getLogger(__name__)
@@ -294,8 +300,26 @@
         self.device.write(buf)
 
         attempts = 0
+        transport_retries = 0
         while True:
-            res = self.device.read(_RESPONSE_LENGTH)
+            try:
+                res = self.device.read(_RESPONSE_LENGTH)
+            except Timeout:
+                # The Commander occasionally drops a response window. Re-sending the
+                # whole command is the only recovery: a read alone would keep timing
+                # out, and 50 such attempts would block the caller for ~50s.
+                transport_retries += 1
+                if transport_retries > 3:
+                    raise
+                _LOGGER.debug(
+                    "read timed out on command %s, re-sending (attempt %d/3)",
+                    command,
+                    transport_retries,
+                )
+                time.sleep(0.1)
+                self.device.clear_enqueued_reports()
+                self.device.write(buf)
+                continue
             # Skip reports with non-0x00 report ID
             if res[0] != 0x00:
                 attempts += 1
